            <div xml:id="d546">

                <pb facs="0802" n="786" sameAs="frus:frus1947v04/pg786"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On April 12, 1947, in Moscow, during the Fourth Session of the Council of Foreign
                    Ministers (March 10–April 24), Edvard Kardelj, Vice President of Yugoslavia and
                    head of the Yugoslav Delegation at the Council of Foreign Ministers, accompanied
                    by Yugoslav Foreign Minister Stanoje Simić, called upon the Secretary of State.
                    In the course of the conversation, which was largely given over to a
                    consideration of the proposed Austrian Peace Treaty, Vice President <pb
                        facs="0803" n="787" xml:id="pg787"/> Kardelj did touch on the wish of his
                    government to improve relations with the United States. For the record of the
                    conversation, see <ref target="frus:frus1947v02/pg_328">volume II, page
                        328</ref>.</p>
            </div>
